// ICF codes, Socialstyrelsen inventory to SNOMED CT mappings, codes b53-b59
// Several sources map to the same target; each mapping is its own assertion.
context {
    collection "icf-snomed-ct" version="2026.1"
    source system="ICF" release="2026"
    target system="SNOMED_CT" release="20251130"
}
defaults {
    mappings {
        preference "primary"
        assessment-method "source-default-granularity"
    }
}
mapping "b530.1" source="b530" target="SNOMED_CT:27113001" relationship=source_is_narrower_than_target {
    confidence 0.03 scheme="vocabmod-se-confidence@1"
    comment "en" """
        Source b530 SNOMED CT 27113001 = ICF b530: the body functions of WEIGHT MAINTENANCE — the
        physiological functions that regulate and maintain appropriate body weight, per WHO ICF
        definition. Target =, active RF2 production 20260701, the SNOMED CT observable that names body
        weight. This is the closest defensible standard concept: no SNOMED CT observable exists (the
        weight-maintenance hits 33861001/388962008 are regimen/therapy concepts, not functions;
        405089001 is a behavior observable, not the maintenance function; 102492002 is a pathological
        finding). 27113001 is the measurable correlate that the maintenance function regulates. Broader
        rather than exact: SNOMED CT models body weight as an OBSERVABLE (a measurement) where ICF b530
        frames it as a FUNCTION (the physiological weight-regulating mechanism), and is broader than —
        the target is the regulated quantity, not the regulating function. Low tier : the closest
        defensible weight-related observable, term-verified active, but a real semantic gap exists
        between the ICF framing and the SNOMED CT measurement observable, and no independent crosswalk
        exists; recorded as the best available lead rather than a strong map.
        """
}
mapping "b535.1" source="b535" target="SNOMED_CT:251378002" relationship=source_is_narrower_than_target effect=omitted quality=60 {
    confidence 0.87 scheme="vocabmod-se-confidence@1"
    comment "en" """
        Source b535 SNOMED CT 251378002 = ICF b535: the body functions of SENSATIONS associated with the
        digestive system — the felt/qualitative sensations arising from digestive-system activity, per
        WHO ICF definition, with children b5350 nausea, b5351 feeling bloated, b5352 abdominal cramp.
        Target =, active RF2 production 20260701, the direct SNOMED CT observable that names the
        gastrointestinal sensation. This is the closest standard equivalent; the valued correlates
        251379005 altered and 251380008 unchanged sit beneath as findings, and 366259001 is the finding
        framing. Broader rather than exact: ICF b535 is a multi-child sensation block (b5350-b5352:
        nausea, bloating, cramp) where is a single observable for the general GI sensation; the target
        sits above the children as the umbrella concept and one level away in model framing (observable
        of sensation vs ICF sensation function). High tier : direct term-and-scope match
        (gastrointestinal sensation = sensations associated with the digestive system) verified active
        in the mirror, one-level-broader in model granularity, no independent Athena crosswalk
        re-verified.
        """
}
mapping "b5350.1" source="b5350" target="SNOMED_CT:422587007" relationship=source_is_narrower_than_target {
    confidence 0.71 scheme="vocabmod-se-confidence@1"
    comment "en" """
        Source b5350 SNOMED CT 422587007 = ICF b5350: the specific body function/sensation of NAUSEA — the
        sensation of feeling sick / the urge to vomit, per WHO ICF definition. Target =, active RF2
        production 20260701, the active SNOMED CT concept that names nausea (the prior concept 73879007 was
        inactivated 2007-01-31 and 422587007 is its active successor in the mirror). This is the closest
        standard equivalent; the related 16932000 bundles vomiting which the source does not. Broader
        rather than exact: SNOMED CT models nausea as a FINDING (clinical observation) where ICF b5350
        frames it as a SENSATION FUNCTION (the physiological felt experience), and the finding fully
        contains the source domain but is one level away in model framing. High tier : direct
        term-and-scope match (nausea = sensation of nausea) verified active in the mirror,
        one-level-broader in model framing, no independent Athena crosswalk re-verified. (Inactive
        73879007 was rejected in favour of its active replacement 422587007.)
        """
}
